[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Test Framework Logging, Reporting, and Assertions"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"A robust test automation framework relies heavily on clear assertions, comprehensive logging, and rich reporting. Together, these pillars provide visibility into test execution, simplify debugging, and ensure reliable validation of application behavior."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Advanced Assertions: Hard vs. Soft Assertions"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Assertions are the core of automated testing, determining whether a test passes or fails. While hard assertions abort test execution immediately upon failure, soft assertions allow the test to continue, collecting multiple failures before reporting."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"SoftAssert softAssert = new SoftAssert();
softAssert.assertEquals(actualTitle, expectedTitle, "Title mismatch");
softAssert.assertTrue(isElementDisplayed, "Element not visible");
softAssert.assertAll();"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Framework Logging with Log4j2"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Effective logging tracks the flow of execution and aids in troubleshooting non-reproducible issues. Log4j2 is the industry standard in Java-based frameworks for recording DEBUG, INFO, WARN, and ERROR events."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"INFO: Tracks major test milestones (e.g., 'Navigating to Login Page')."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"DEBUG: Captures granular parameters, locators, and state changes."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ERROR: Logs exceptions, failed element lookups, and timeouts."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"private static final Logger logger = LogManager.getLogger(LoginTest.class);

public void login(String username, String password) {
    logger.info("Entering username: " + username);
    driver.findElement(By.id("username")).sendKeys(username);
    logger.info("Entering password");
    driver.findElement(By.id("password")).sendKeys(password);
    driver.findElement(By.id("submit")).click();
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Rich HTML Reporting with ExtentReports"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"ExtentReports provides an interactive HTML report detailing test steps, device information, screenshots, and logs. It transforms raw console outputs into professional stakeholder-ready documentation."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"ExtentSparkReporter spark = new ExtentSparkReporter("target/ExtentReport.html");
ExtentReports extent = new ExtentReports();
extent.attachReporter(spark);

ExtentTest test = extent.createTest("Login Validation Test");
test.pass("Login successful");
test.fail("Dashboard not loaded", MediaEntityBuilder.createScreenCaptureFromPath("screenshot.png").build());
extent.flush();"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Advanced Analytics with Allure Report"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"Allure is a flexible, lightweight multi-language test report tool that shows a very concise representation of what has been tested in a web-based dashboard, featuring step breakdowns, attachments, history, and severity levels."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"@Step("Type username {0} and password")
public void enterCredentials(String user, String pass) {
    Allure.addAttachment("Environment", "QA");
    driver.findElement(By.id("username")).sendKeys(user);
    driver.findElement(By.id("password")).sendKeys(pass);
}"},{"order":18,"type":"subheading","text":"Summary"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"By integrating soft assertions, detailed Log4j2 tracking, and visually engaging Extent or Allure reporting, your automation suite will achieve enterprise-grade reliability and maintainability."}]
